-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1: sections 142 and 143 -- OFFICERS; LOANS TO EMPLOYEES AND OFFICERS.
--
-- SEAT: an officer, a director, a stockholder. Cross-references taken as inputs: sections 103(a)(2) (piece dg1) and 158 (piece dg3),
-- how instruments and stock certificates are signed. The text is de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (a plain-text rendering, not the official text).

§ `Section 142(a): the officers a corporation must have`

-- "Every corporation organized under this chapter shall have such officers with such titles and duties as shall be stated in the bylaws
-- or in a resolution of the board of directors which is not inconsistent with the bylaws". A statement in the certificate is not one of
-- the two places the text names: not covered. A statement nowhere: not stated.
-- src:383 | Every corporation organized under this chapter shall have such officers with such titles and duties as shall be stated in the bylaws or in a resolution of the board of directors which is not inconsistent with the bylaws …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 142(a) (src:383)
GIVEN `where the titles and duties of the officers are stated` IS A `Where a provision is made`
      `the resolution is inconsistent with the bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 142(a) the titles and duties of the officers are stated as the Law requires` `where the titles and duties of the officers are stated` `the resolution is inconsistent with the bylaws` MEANS
    CONSIDER `where the titles and duties of the officers are stated`
    WHEN `in the bylaws` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `in a resolution of the board of directors` THEN JUST (NOT `the resolution is inconsistent with the bylaws`)
    WHEN `in the certificate of incorporation` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `in none of these` THEN JUST FALSE

-- "...and as may be necessary to enable it to sign instruments and stock certificates which comply with §§ 103(a)(2) and 158 of this
-- title." Whether the instruments and certificates comply with sections 103(a)(2) and 158 is for dg1 and dg3: a fact here.
-- out of range: section 103(a)(2) (piece dg1) and section 158 (piece dg3): what makes an instrument or a certificate comply is theirs; whether the officers suffice is a plain input.
-- src:383 | and as may be necessary to enable it to sign instruments and stock certificates which comply with §§ 103(a)(2) and 158 of this title. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 142(a) (src:383)
GIVEN `the officers are enough to enable the corporation to sign the instruments and stock certificates which comply with sections 103(a)(2) and 158` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 142(a) the corporation has the officers it needs to sign instruments and stock certificates` `the officers are enough to enable the corporation to sign the instruments and stock certificates which comply with sections 103(a)(2) and 158` MEANS
    `the officers are enough to enable the corporation to sign the instruments and stock certificates which comply with sections 103(a)(2) and 158`

-- "One of the officers shall have the duty to record the proceedings of the meetings of the stockholders and directors in a book to be
-- kept for that purpose."
-- src:383 | One of the officers shall have the duty to record the proceedings of the meetings of the stockholders and directors in a book to be kept for that purpose. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 142(a) (src:383)
GIVEN `the number of officers who have the duty to record the proceedings of the meetings of the stockholders and directors in a book` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 142(a) one of the officers has the duty to record the proceedings of the meetings` `the number of officers who have the duty to record the proceedings of the meetings of the stockholders and directors in a book` MEANS
    `the number of officers who have the duty to record the proceedings of the meetings of the stockholders and directors in a book` AT LEAST 1

-- "Any number of offices may be held by the same person unless the certificate of incorporation or bylaws otherwise provide."
-- src:383 | Any number of offices may be held by the same person unless the certificate of incorporation or bylaws otherwise provide.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 142(a) (src:383)
GIVEN `where it is otherwise provided` IS A `Where a provision is made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 142(a) the same person may hold any number of offices` `where it is otherwise provided` MEANS
    NOT (`dg2 the place is the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws` `where it is otherwise provided`)

§ `Section 142(b) to (e): choosing, holding, resigning, bonding, vacancies`

-- "Officers shall be chosen in such manner and shall hold their offices for such terms as are prescribed by the bylaws or determined by
-- the board of directors or other governing body."
-- src:384 | Officers shall be chosen in such manner and shall hold their offices for such terms as are prescribed by the bylaws or determined by the board of directors or other governing body. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 142(b) (src:384)
GIVEN `the manner of choosing and the term are prescribed by the bylaws` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the manner of choosing and the term are determined by the board of directors or other governing body` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 142(b) the manner of choosing the officers and their terms are fixed as the Law provides` `the manner of choosing and the term are prescribed by the bylaws` `the manner of choosing and the term are determined by the board of directors or other governing body` MEANS
        `the manner of choosing and the term are prescribed by the bylaws`
    OR  `the manner of choosing and the term are determined by the board of directors or other governing body`

-- "Each officer shall hold office until such officer's successor is elected and qualified or until such officer's earlier resignation or removal."
-- src:384 | Each officer shall hold office until such officer’s successor is elected and qualified or until such officer’s earlier resignation or removal. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 142(b) (src:384)
GIVEN `a successor has been elected and has qualified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has resigned` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the officer has been removed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 142(b) the officer still holds office` `a successor has been elected and has qualified` `the officer has resigned` `the officer has been removed` MEANS
    NOT (   `a successor has been elected and has qualified`
         OR `the officer has resigned`
         OR `the officer has been removed`)

-- "Any officer may resign at any time upon written notice to the corporation." The text names written notice only (not electronic
-- transmission, which section 141(b) names for a director): whether an electronic transmission is the equivalent of a written document
-- is section 116 (piece dg1). Without written notice the text does not say how an officer resigns.
-- src:384 | Any officer may resign at any time upon written notice to the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 142(b) (src:384)
GIVEN `the officer gave written notice of the resignation to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 142(b) the officer may resign` `the officer gave written notice of the resignation to the corporation` MEANS
    IF   `the officer gave written notice of the resignation to the corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "The corporation may secure the fidelity of any or all of its officers or agents by bond or otherwise."
-- src:385 | (c) The corporation may secure the fidelity of any or all of its officers or agents by bond or otherwise.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 142(c) (src:385)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or an agent of the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 142(c) the corporation may secure the fidelity of the person by bond or otherwise` `the person is an officer or an agent of the corporation` MEANS
    IF   `the person is an officer or an agent of the corporation`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

-- "A failure to elect officers shall not dissolve or otherwise affect the corporation."
-- src:386 | (d) A failure to elect officers shall not dissolve or otherwise affect the corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 142(d) (src:386)
GIVEN `the corporation has failed to elect officers` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 142(d) the failure to elect officers dissolves or otherwise affects the corporation` `the corporation has failed to elect officers` MEANS
    FALSE

DECLARE `s 142(e) Who fills a vacancy` IS ONE OF
    `as the bylaws provide`
    `the board of directors or other governing body`

-- "Any vacancy occurring in any office of the corporation by death, resignation, removal or otherwise, shall be filled as the bylaws
-- provide. In the absence of such provision, the vacancy shall be filled by the board of directors or other governing body."
-- src:387 | (e) Any vacancy occurring in any office of the corporation by death, resignation, removal or otherwise, shall be filled as the bylaws provide. In the absence of such provision, the vacancy shall be filled by the board of directors or other governing body.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 142(e) (src:387)
GIVEN `the bylaws provide how the vacancy is to be filled` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 142(e) Who fills a vacancy`
`s 142(e) how the vacancy in the office is filled` `the bylaws provide how the vacancy is to be filled` MEANS
    IF   `the bylaws provide how the vacancy is to be filled`
    THEN `as the bylaws provide`
    ELSE `the board of directors or other governing body`

§ `Section 143: loans to employees and officers`

-- "Any corporation may lend money to, or guarantee any obligation of, or otherwise assist any officer or other employee of the
-- corporation or of its subsidiary, including any officer or employee who is a director of the corporation or its subsidiary, whenever,
-- in the judgment of the directors, such loan, guaranty or assistance may reasonably be expected to benefit the corporation."
-- The judgment is the directors': an input.
-- src:391 | Any corporation may lend money to, or guarantee any obligation of, or otherwise assist any officer or other employee of the corporation or of its subsidiary, including any officer or employee who is a director of the corporation or its subsidiary, whenever, in the judgment of the directors, such loan, guaranty or assistance may reasonably be expected to benefit the corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 143 (src:391)
GIVEN `the person is an officer or other employee of the corporation or of its subsidiary, including one who is a director of the corporation or its subsidiary` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in the judgment of the directors the loan, guaranty or assistance may reasonably be expected to benefit the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 143 the corporation may lend money to, guarantee an obligation of, or otherwise assist the person` `the person is an officer or other employee of the corporation or of its subsidiary, including one who is a director of the corporation or its subsidiary` `in the judgment of the directors the loan, guaranty or assistance may reasonably be expected to benefit the corporation` MEANS
        `the person is an officer or other employee of the corporation or of its subsidiary, including one who is a director of the corporation or its subsidiary`
    AND `in the judgment of the directors the loan, guaranty or assistance may reasonably be expected to benefit the corporation`

-- "The loan, guaranty or other assistance may be with or without interest, and may be unsecured, or secured in such manner as the board
-- of directors shall approve, including, without limitation, a pledge of shares of stock of the corporation."
DECLARE `s 143 How the loan is secured` IS ONE OF
    `unsecured`
    `secured in a manner the board of directors approves`
    `secured by a pledge of shares of stock of the corporation, a manner the board of directors approves`
    `secured in a manner the board of directors has not approved`

-- src:391 | The loan, guaranty or other assistance may be with or without interest, and may be unsecured, or secured in such manner as the board of directors shall approve, including, without limitation, a pledge of shares of stock of the corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 143 (src:391)
GIVEN `the loan bears interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 143 the loan, guaranty or other assistance may be with or without interest` `the loan bears interest` MEANS
    TRUE

-- src:391 | and may be unsecured, or secured in such manner as the board of directors shall approve, including, without limitation, a pledge of shares of stock of the corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 143 (src:391)
GIVEN `the security` IS A `s 143 How the loan is secured`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 143 the loan, guaranty or other assistance may be secured in this way` `the security` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the security`
    WHEN `unsecured` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `secured in a manner the board of directors approves` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `secured by a pledge of shares of stock of the corporation, a manner the board of directors approves` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `secured in a manner the board of directors has not approved` THEN FALSE

-- "Nothing in this section contained shall be deemed to deny, limit or restrict the powers of guaranty or warranty of any corporation at
-- common law or under any statute."
-- src:391 | Nothing in this section contained shall be deemed to deny, limit or restrict the powers of guaranty or warranty of any corporation at common law or under any statute.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 143 (src:391)
GIVEN `the power of guaranty or warranty is one the corporation has at common law or under a statute` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 143 this section denies, limits or restricts the power` `the power of guaranty or warranty is one the corporation has at common law or under a statute` MEANS
